---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE, DEFAULT_OG, fmtDate, iso, POSTS } from "../../lib/blog.mjs";

const slug = "wix-vs-custom-code-blog";
const idx = POSTS.findIndex((p) => p.slug === slug);
const post = POSTS[idx];
const next = POSTS[(idx + 1) % POSTS.length];

const canonical = `${SITE}/blog/${slug}/`;
const ogImage = post.coverImage ? `${SITE}${post.coverImage}` : DEFAULT_OG;
const primaryTag = post.tags[0] || "Notes";
const readMins = post.readMins;
const showUpdated = post.updatedDate && +new Date(post.updatedDate) > +new Date(post.pubDate);
const updatedLabel = showUpdated ? `Updated ${fmtDate(post.updatedDate)}` : null;

const jsonld = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BlogPosting",
      "@id": `${canonical}#post`,
      headline: post.title,
      description: post.description,
      datePublished: iso(post.pubDate),
      dateModified: iso(post.updatedDate || post.pubDate),
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Divyansh Sood", url: `${SITE}/`, "@id": `${SITE}/#person` },
      publisher: {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "@id": `${SITE}/#studio`,
        name: "Divyansh Sood® Studio",
        logo: { "@type": "ImageObject", url: `${SITE}/icon.svg` },
      },
      isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", "@id": `${SITE}/#website` },
      mainEntityOfPage: { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": canonical },
      image: ogImage,
      articleSection: primaryTag,
      keywords: post.tags.join(", "),
      wordCount: 975,
      timeRequired: `PT${readMins}M`,
      speakable: {
        "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
        cssSelector: [".post-title", ".post-lead"],
      },
      inLanguage: "en",
      url: canonical,
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Blog", item: `${SITE}/blog/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: post.title, item: canonical },
      ],
    },
  ],
});
---

<Layout
  title={post.seoTitle ?? `${post.title} · Divyansh Sood`}
  description={post.description}
  canonical={canonical}
  keywords={post.tags.join(", ")}
  ogType="article"
  ogTitle={post.title}
  ogImage={ogImage}
  ogImageW={1200}
  ogImageH={750}
  articlePublished={iso(post.pubDate)}
  articleModified={iso(post.updatedDate || post.pubDate)}
  tags={post.tags}
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <header class="post-hero">
      <div class="post-hero-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          <span>{primaryTag}</span>
          <span>{fmtDate(post.pubDate)}</span>
          {updatedLabel && <span class="post-updated">{updatedLabel}</span>}
          <span>{readMins} min read</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="post-title">{post.title}</h1>
        <p class="post-lead">{post.description}</p>
        <div class="post-meta">
          <span>By Divyansh Sood</span><span>{fmtDate(post.pubDate)}</span><span>{readMins} min read</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    {post.coverImage && (
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <figure class="post-cover">
          <img src={post.coverImage} alt={post.title} width="1200" height="750" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
        </figure>
      </div>
    )}

    <article class="wrap narrow post-body">
      <p>Every week, someone messages me with the same question:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>“Divyansh bhai, Wix toh free hai — why should I pay ₹13,000?”</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Fair question. Let me answer it properly — no sales pitch, just what actually happens when a real business uses each one.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="first-what-wix-actually-gives-you">First, what Wix actually gives you</h2>
<p>Wix works. I’m not going to pretend it doesn’t. You can sign up, drag things around, and have something that looks like a website in an afternoon.</p>
<p>But here’s what you’re actually signing up for:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Their subdomain</strong> (yourbusiness.wixsite.com) until you pay for a domain</li>
<li><strong>Their branding</strong> in your footer — even on paid plans</li>
<li><strong>Their servers</strong> — which you share with thousands of other sites</li>
<li><strong>Their templates</strong> — which your competitor three towns over is probably also using</li>
<li><strong>Their rules</strong> — if they change pricing, kill a feature, or shut down your plan, you have no exit</li>
</ul>
<p>You don’t own anything. You’re renting a shop inside someone else’s mall.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="what-actually-hurts-you-on-google">What actually hurts you on Google</h2>
<p>This is the part nobody talks about honestly.</p>
<p>Wix has improved over the years — Google can crawl it now, yes. But “Google can crawl it” is not the same as “Google will rank it.”</p>
<p>Here’s what Wix still gets wrong for most Indian SMEs:</p>
<p><strong>Page speed.</strong> Wix loads a lot of JavaScript by default — animations, their editor logic, tracking scripts. On a mobile connection in Palampur or Pathankot, that adds up. Google’s Core Web Vitals score suffers. Your ranking suffers with it.</p>
<p><strong>Code bloat.</strong> Every Wix page ships HTML and CSS for features you never turned on. A custom site ships only what’s on the page.</p>
<p><strong>Schema markup.</strong> If you’re a tour operator, a clinic, or a local business — Google rewards structured data (business name, hours, reviews, service areas). Wix gives you limited control over this. A custom build lets me wire in JSON-LD schema that directly tells Google what your business is and where it operates.</p>
<p><strong>llms.txt.</strong> This one is newer. AI search engines — ChatGPT, Perplexity, Claude — now crawl websites differently from Google. A file called <code>llms.txt</code> tells them exactly what your site is about. Wix doesn’t support this. Every custom site I ship has one.</p>
<p>One of my clients, InHimalayas, saw a sudden surge in AI-referred traffic within weeks of launch — because the site was built for AI crawlers from day one. That’s not possible on Wix.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="so-what-does-13000-actually-build">So what does ₹13,000 actually build?</h2>
<p>The Starter package — ₹13,000 to ₹16,000 — is a 5-page custom-coded site. Here’s what that means in practice:</p>
<p><strong>5 pages:</strong> Home, About, Services, Gallery, Contact. Everything a service business needs. Nothing it doesn’t.</p>
<p><strong>Custom layout.</strong> Not a template. Not something your competitor can buy for ₹500/month. Every section is built for your business specifically.</p>
<p><strong>WhatsApp-first contact form.</strong> Every enquiry goes to your WhatsApp AND your email simultaneously. No lead falls through. This alone has changed the conversion rate for every client I’ve worked with.</p>
<p><strong>Lighthouse 90+ on mobile.</strong> This is a Google-audited performance score. 90+ means your site loads fast, is accessible, and passes Core Web Vitals. Most Wix sites score in the 50s–70s on mobile.</p>
<p><strong>SEO basics done right.</strong> Meta titles, descriptions, Open Graph tags, sitemap, robots.txt, and JSON-LD schema — all set up at launch, not as an afterthought.</p>
<p><strong>Free hosting for year 1.</strong> On Vercel. Faster than shared hosting. No ads. No Wix branding. Yours.</p>
<p><strong>Delivered in 14 days.</strong> Brief to live URL. Not 6 months. Not “we’ll get back to you after discovery.”</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="the-real-comparison-side-by-side">The real comparison, side by side</h2>


















































<table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Wix (paid plan)</th><th>Custom — ₹13K</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Monthly cost</td><td>₹800–2,500/month</td><td>₹0 (year 1 hosting free)</td></tr><tr><td>You own the code</td><td>✗</td><td>✓</td></tr><tr><td>Mobile Lighthouse score</td><td>50–70</td><td>90+</td></tr><tr><td>WhatsApp lead form</td><td>Plugin needed</td><td>Built in</td></tr><tr><td>Schema / JSON-LD</td><td>Limited</td><td>Full control</td></tr><tr><td>llms.txt (AI search)</td><td>✗</td><td>✓</td></tr><tr><td>Looks like a template</td><td>Often yes</td><td>Never</td></tr><tr><td>Exit anytime</td><td>Hard</td><td>Easy — your code, your server</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Over 3 years, a Wix Business plan costs you ₹28,000–90,000. And at the end of it, you still don’t own anything.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="when-wix-makes-sense">When Wix makes sense</h2>
<p>I’ll be straight: Wix is fine if —</p>
<ul>
<li>You’re testing a business idea and need something up in 24 hours</li>
<li>You’ll be updating content yourself every day and can’t wait on a developer</li>
<li>You genuinely have no budget and need literally anything</li>
</ul>
<p>But if you’re a real business — a tour operator, a clinic, a school, a D2C brand — and you want Google to find you, customers to trust you, and leads to actually reach you: Wix is a ceiling, not a launchpad.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="what-i-tell-clients">What I tell clients</h2>
<p>A website is not a brochure. It’s a sales tool.</p>
<p>A brochure sits in a drawer. A sales tool generates enquiries at 2 AM while you’re asleep.</p>
<p>Wix can make a brochure. A custom site — built fast, built right, built for how Indian customers actually search and message — can be a sales tool.</p>
<p>That’s the difference. That’s what ₹13,000 gets you.</p>
<hr>
<p><em>I’m Divyansh, solo developer out of Kangra Valley. Custom-coded websites for Indian small businesses — from ₹13,000, live in 14 days. WhatsApp reply in under an hour, 9 AM–9 PM IST. <a href="https://wa.me/919816091875">Drop me a message</a> and I’ll tell you within a day whether a custom build makes sense for what you’re running — or point you at someone who’d be a better fit if it doesn’t.</em></p>
<p><em>See real examples: <a href="https://www.divyanshsood.com/projects/dharamshala-tours">Dharamshala Tours</a> — WhatsApp-first, custom CMS, ~1,000 bookings/month. <a href="https://www.divyanshsood.com/projects/nandini">Nandini Travels</a> — rebuilt from a broken site to direct bookings in under 2 weeks.</em></p>
      <div class="tags">{post.tags.map((t) => <span>{t}</span>)}</div>
    </article>

    <section class="wrap narrow" aria-label="Keep reading">
      <a class="post-next" href={`/blog/${next.slug}/`}>
        <span><span class="label">Read next</span><br /><span class="name">{next.title}</span></span>
        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="post-foot-cta">
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        {post.audience === "indian-smb" ? (
          <>
            <h2>Working on something in India?</h2>
            <p>If a post here matches what you're building, send me the brief. WhatsApp reply in under an hour, 9 AM–9 PM IST — I'll tell you within a day if it's a fit.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://wa.me/919816091875" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Message me on WhatsApp <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#work">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : post.audience === "d2c-brand" ? (
          <>
            <h2>Building a brand a theme can't carry?</h2>
            <p>If your store has a model that off-the-shelf builders fight — hand-numbered drops, creator commerce, premium D2C — tell me about it. I read every brief personally.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com"
                >Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#work">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <h2>Working on something similar?</h2>
            <p>If a post here matches what you're building, send me the brief. I reply personally, usually within a couple of hours — and I'll tell you within a day if it's a fit.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com"
                >Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://calendly.com/sood-divyansh007/30min" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Book a 15-min intro <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
            </div>
          </>
        )}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
